WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.468
 Gentlemen, congratulations.

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.170
It's down to the two
of you to decide who's

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.405
going to leave here with the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.941
champion and that
check for $10,000.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.942
Now, in this final round,
we're sending you back

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:11.878
to your home forges
for four days

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.913
to build an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.082
We want you to build this.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:18.351
[suspenseful music]

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.185
 Oh.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:24.523
 This is the
elephant tusk sword.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.860
NARRATOR: Dating as far
back as the 6th century BC,

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.328
the mighty elephant was
used during warfare,

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:32.165
often armed with the
fierce elephant tusk sword.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:35.134
This lethal weapon featured a
socket that connected directly

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.703
to the elephant's tusk.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.037
The double-edged
blade was designed

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.173
to inflict massive
destruction as an elephant

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.275
charged through barricades
and ranks of enemy soldiers.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:44.811
Throughout history,
there's evidence

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.713
of thousands of elephant tusk
swords being used in battle.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.683
However, only four pairs of
these intimidating weapons

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:51.851
still exist today.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.419
 I've never seen
anything like it.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:56.088
I'm trying to figure out how I'm
even going to construct this.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.691
A terrifying feeling is
starting to set in again.

00:00:58.791 --> 00:00:59.725
 Good luck.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:00.426
We'll see you in four days.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:01.327
 Hell, yeah.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.932 line:14%
 My name is Matt [inaudible].

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.234 line:8%
I'm 38 years old from
Knoxville, Tennessee.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:11.103 line:8%
I'm a senior engineer and
a part-time bladesmith.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.739
I'm not normally
a competitive guy.

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.507
But for this, I
made an exception.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.641
Because I'm here to win.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.144
My adrenaline's already
pumping through my veins.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.645
And I'm ready for
that challenge.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.480
I've got my width
that I'm looking for.

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:24.184
But my workpiece might
be a little too thin.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:28.921 line:8%
I'm going to try and forge weld
in a mild steel medial ridge.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.623 line:8%
So I'm going to
get some mild steel

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.326 line:8%
and try and forge weld
that onto both sides.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.026
All right.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.161
Now, we're cooking.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.762
This sword is meant
for an elephant.

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:39.332
So the amount of force that's
going to go into the blade

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.400
is going to be off the charts.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.936
We want as even of a
heat as we can get.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.170
Check it with a magnet.

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:46.806
Make sure that we're
at a critical temp,

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:52.044
and then pull it out,
drop it in my quench oil.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:55.114
Good so far.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:56.916
[suspenseful music]

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.217
I don't see any cracks.

00:01:58.283 --> 00:02:01.653
All the welds held up,
nothing blew apart.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.755
So far, so good.

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.924
Now, just to make
it look pretty.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.059
I'm going to start
off by securing

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:09.062
the blade to the socket.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.330
I'm worried about possibly
overheating the blade.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.232
So I'm going to have
to take some extra care

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:14.934
to make sure the heat
doesn't travel and ruin

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.636
the temper on the blade.

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:18.271
Let that cool off.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:21.540
Doing a kind of test
fit of the sword.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.575
Perfect.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.810
Everything goes
together smooth as silk.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.946
This blade is crazy.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.048
I never would have
imagined myself

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.550
making something like this.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.418
So I'm kind of excited to
see what kind of destruction

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:34.420
it does or maybe the
sword blows apart.

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:35.555
I don't know.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.057 line:14%
Looks pretty sweet.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.526 line:14%
 My name's Jayden [inaudible].

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:40.626 line:14%
I'm 19 years old.

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:43.296 line:8%
And I started bladesmithing
at about age 15.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.965
My entire life, I've gotten
in trouble for two things--

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.734
playing with knives
and playing with fire.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.237
And so eventually,
it clicked in my mind

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.973
that I could make
knives with fire.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.342
And it really just
went from there.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.444
Everything's looking good.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.446
I think that it's
all welded up well.

00:03:00.512 --> 00:03:03.015
I'm going to start
preparing to weld

00:03:03.081 --> 00:03:04.817
the socket cap onto the blade.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:08.654
If I do these welds incorrectly,
I will end up with cracks.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.322
I could end up with
the whole blade,

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:13.826
basically, just breaking off.

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:16.563
[rock music]

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.332
The welds ended up great.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:22.001
So I'm feeling good
about where I am.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.670
And today's mostly just going to
be making this thing beautiful.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.972
So I think I'm going to
grind it like I would an ax.

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.807
I'm going to do
big convex edges.

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:31.744
Because all of that extra meat
in there will help support

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.179
the cutting edge itself.

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:34.714
That's exactly how I wanted it.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.882
It's way cooler than I ever
thought it would have been.

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:38.484
And I'm happy with it.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:39.852
At this point, I could show up.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.654
And on the first hit,
it could snap in half

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:42.988
and I'd walk away happy.

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.257
I hope it doesn't, though.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:45.358
I do want to win.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.426
[laughs]

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.296
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:53.165
In battle, these swords were
attached to elephants who just

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.368
rammed across its opponents.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.603
Find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do.

00:03:57.703 --> 00:04:00.439
We're going to go hog-wild
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.574
Jayden, you're up first.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.641
You ready for this?
- Hell, yeah.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:03.509
 Let's do this.

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:08.748
 Ooh.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:09.582
Oh.

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:15.855
Ah.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:23.061
I wasn't expecting
his head to come off.

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:24.296
 All right.

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.065
Jayden, let's talk
about your weapon here.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.200
Every thrust was deadly.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.935
It went all the way through.

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:33.972
What I do like is I can see the
Damascus pattern on your blade

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:35.307
there.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:39.344
Jayden, your elephant
tusk sword, it will kill.

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:40.379
 That's all I wanted.

00:04:40.445 --> 00:04:41.314
 All right.
Matt, your turn.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.881
So are you ready?

00:04:42.981 --> 00:04:45.050
 Hopefully, my sword is not
"irrelephant" after this test.

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.152
[laughter]

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:49.022
 We're going to have fun.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:51.291
[suspenseful music]

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.294
MATT: Ooh.

00:05:04.469 --> 00:05:06.505
 All right, Matt, it
penetrates very deep.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:09.108
And on the way out, it cuts.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.542
It's a weighted
weapon right here

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:11.944
that when it
thrust-- see the hole

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.512
right in the middle of
the ballistics dummy--

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:14.714
it destroyed
everything in there.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.316
Your weapon right
here, it will kill.

00:05:17.382 --> 00:05:18.318
 Thank you, Doug.

00:05:22.487 --> 00:05:24.424
 All right, gentlemen,
the strength test--

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.493
we've mounted your elephant
tusk swords on our battering ram

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.594
here.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:31.096
And I will be attacking
that armored soldier.

00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:32.097
All right.

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:33.032
Jayden, you ready for this?

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:33.766
 Yeah, let's do it.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:36.602
DAVID BAKER: OK.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:37.603
[clank]

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:39.472
 Ooh.

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:40.139
[clank]

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:40.973
 Ooh.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.350
That's terrifying.

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.353
 Jayden, I really
have to commend you

00:05:54.453 --> 00:05:55.587
on the artistry of this blade.

00:05:55.654 --> 00:05:57.823
The low-layer
pattern really pops.

00:05:57.923 --> 00:06:01.327
The connections here are
all really beautifully done.

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:04.396
And for this test, that
tip still has an edge.

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:06.432
Everything is right
and tight and true,

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.167
and nothing's changed.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:08.900
Well done.

00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:10.136
 Thank you.

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.471
- Matt, you ready to roll?
- Absolutely.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:12.372
 OK.

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:16.743
[suspenseful music]

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.049
[clank]

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:36.328
So, Matt, your
blade held up fine.

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:39.098
The tip, it's a
little bit duller

00:06:39.164 --> 00:06:40.599
than when it started out with.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:43.468
But I wouldn't run my finger
down this edge, so nicely done.

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:44.336
It held up beautifully.

00:06:44.403 --> 00:06:45.405
 Thank you.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.442
 All right, bladesmiths, we
know your weapons can kill.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:51.944
And we know they are strong.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:54.146
Now, it's time to find out
how sharp your weapons are.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:58.384
This is the sharpness test,
the guillotine fruit slice.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.686
We're going to take your
elephant tusk sword,

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:03.256
release it, and try to
cut through the fruit.

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:06.225
I want to see clean cuts
all the way through.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:07.393
Jayden, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:07.459 --> 00:07:08.360
- Hell, yeah.
- All right.

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:09.429
Let's do this.

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:21.707
JAYDEN: Nice.

00:07:21.807 --> 00:07:24.609
 All right, Jayden,
your edge here cut

00:07:24.676 --> 00:07:26.412
all the way through cleanly.

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:31.417
Bottom line, sir, your elephant
tusk sword, it will cut.

00:07:31.483 --> 00:07:32.418
All right, Matt, your turn, sir.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.218
You ready?

00:07:33.318 --> 00:07:34.086
 I'm ready.

00:07:38.056 --> 00:07:39.992
[rock music]

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:44.663
MATT: [exhales]

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.232
 All right, Matt, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:07:46.298 --> 00:07:50.336
The weight on this, it drives
the cut all the way through.

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:51.737
Your edge is sharp.

00:07:51.803 --> 00:07:54.807
More importantly,
sir, it will cut.

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:57.276
 Thank you, Doug.

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:58.677
 Well, Jayden
and Matt, you guys

00:07:58.777 --> 00:08:00.412
both performed exceptionally
well during your tests.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:01.947
But as you know,
only one of you guys

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:03.716
will be leaving here with
the title of "Forged in Fire"

00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:04.950
champion.

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:09.055
And today's "Forged in
Fire" champion is Jayden.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.556
Congratulations, you won, man.

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:11.724
Matt, unfortunately,
that means you

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.025
did not come out on top today.

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:15.661
I'm going to have to ask
you to please step out.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:18.563
 I'm proud of the
sword that I turned in.

00:08:18.663 --> 00:08:21.299
They were virtually
the same performance.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.067
Good job, man.

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:23.369
 Yeah, you too.

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:26.438
 And Jayden's weapon, he
turned in a work of art.

00:08:26.538 --> 00:08:29.108
And I think he
deserves the title.

00:08:29.174 --> 00:08:32.044
First thing I'm going to do
when I get home, kiss my wife

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:33.746
and crack open a beer.

00:08:33.812 --> 00:08:37.282
 Well, Jayden, that means you
are today's "Forged in Fire"

00:08:37.349 --> 00:08:38.884
champion.

00:08:38.984 --> 00:08:40.185
You're going to be leaving here
with a check for $10,000, man.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:41.019
Congratulations.

00:08:41.119 --> 00:08:41.921
 Thank you.

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:43.088
[applause]

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:45.091
I'm the newest "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:46.325
And I'm really stoked about it.

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:47.192
 How old are you again?

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:47.960
 19.

00:08:48.027 --> 00:08:49.294
 19 years old--

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:50.896
that is extremely
impressive, man.

00:08:50.996 --> 00:08:51.664
 Thank you.

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:52.331
Whoo!

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:54.800
I'm so bad at emotion.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:55.635
[laughs]

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:58.671
[music playing]

